  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Machines pane filter now offers Waterjet, Wire EDM and Sinker EDM.\nThe existing four kinds keep their indices.\nThe same entries also supply the kind for New blank.\nThe decision file records the scope and alternatives.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe private filter table still listed only the first four machine kinds.\nThe library accepts seven kinds.\n\n## Tests\n\nPin: `the_kind_filter_offers_every_machine_kind_and_filters_its_rows`.\nThe structural test opens the dropdown and checks all seven entries.\nIt selects each kind and checks the visible machine rows.\nThe pin failed on unchanged code because the Waterjet entry was absent.\nThe pin passed after the fix.\nMutation: restored the upstream production file and confirmed failure.\nRestored the fix and confirmed success.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 877 tests passed and six were ignored.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No G-code or CL files changed.\n\n## Before and after\n\nThe images show the Machines pane with its kind dropdown open.\nThe before image uses the original four-kind table.\nThe after image uses the seven-kind table at the PR head.\nBoth images use the same shell and the egui test renderer.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Machines dropdown before the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0854dd03e3e8b43f4a8e9473277cca6c0ed55f0e/2061/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Machines dropdown after the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/0854dd03e3e8b43f4a8e9473277cca6c0ed55f0e/2061/after.png)\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNative window interaction, golden snapshot comparisons and the release gate were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found for the changed paths.\n\nEffort: low. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: Add Waterjet and EDM kinds to the Machines pane filter.\n\nFixes #2030\n\n",
